Z||000000||kinboyatuwo||10-09-2001||12:22 PM||||Since i am here i may as well ask.  Other problems to attend to first but what under hard accel it feels like the rear end is floating and off to one side, makes the car hard to handle, especially in corners (scary)<BR>this is a duke, so no its not fish tailing!<P>any ideas, have to replace the control arm bushings in the front and ball joints, would this have an effect<P>kin<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/b4lower50.jpg"> <BR>"Friends don't let friends drive four doors."<P>87 Duke, 235,000km||||reg||1
Z||000001||PBJ||10-09-2001||06:54 PM||||Before, when the upper control arm bushings were loose mine would pull hard left on accell and between/during shifts I would drift right.  You will need to check out the frt end suspesion and steering and rear suspension. ie ball joints and tie rod ends and control arm bushings.<P>Pete.||||reg||1
Z||000002||mbramble||10-09-2001||07:10 PM||||When mine drove like that, a 4 wheel alignment took care of it.  It <I>was</I> scarey before!!||||reg||1
